1
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:09,240
Dormant leads rarely die because someone said no. They die because nobody followed up.

2
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:15,240
A lead fills out a form, has one conversation, and then goes quiet. Maybe they got busy.

3
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:19,240
Maybe the timing was wrong. Maybe the budget wasn't there yet.

4
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:25,240
Three months later they're still in the CRM, still reachable, and completely forgotten.

5
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:31,240
Your team is focused on this week's leads, because this week's leads are the ones in front of them.

6
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:39,240
So the leads you already paid to acquire just sit there, going colder, while the ad budget keeps buying new ones.

7
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:42,240
Worry not, I'm here to close your loop.

8
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:47,240
Here's the fix. It runs on a schedule, so nobody has to remember.

9
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:53,240
First, it pulls dormant leads from the CRM, anyone not touched in a set number of days.

10
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:56,240
Then, for each one it gathers the context.

11
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:02,240
Who they are, what they asked about, what was said last time, that context goes to an AI model,

12
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:07,240
which writes a short, personal check-in. Not a blast, not a template.

13
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:11,240
One message per lead, referencing the actual conversation.

14
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:17,240
Each message is filed as a Gmail draft. So a human reads it before anything goes out.

15
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:19,240
And here's the part that matters.

16
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:24,240
The workflow marks each lead as drafted, and tracks it in the CRM.

17
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:31,240
So a lead is never messaged twice, and your team can see exactly who's been woken up, and who replied.

18
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:35,240
No spam, no duplicate outreach, no lead left behind.

19
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:40,240
Wake the leads you already paid for, bring your CRM and your definition of dormant.

20
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:44,240
And I'll show you how many conversations you're sitting on.

21
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:47,240
I'm Christian, n8n automation architect.

22
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,240
Book a discovery call now.
